Purpose:
This process document defines the operational procedures for designing, developing, and executing performance test scripts using Apache JMeter. It also outlines how to collect and document performance results for analysis and reporting purposes.



Recommended Revision of Section 6.0
Using Apache JMeter, performance tests are created to simulate real-world load by defining user behavior and events that occur during a testing session. JMeter generates load using virtual users, allowing consistent and repeatable testing by emulating typical user interactions on the system under test.
The performance testing process includes the following key phases:
Designing the test: Define the scope, goals, and expected load. Set up test environments and identify key business transactions to simulate.
Creating the script: Develop JMeter test plans by modeling end-user behavior using samplers, controllers, timers, and extractors.
Executing the test: Run the JMeter test plan, either locally or in a distributed mode. Monitor system metrics and ensure proper load generation.
Analyzing results: Use listeners and external integrations (e.g., InfluxDB/Grafana) to evaluate performance trends, identify bottlenecks, and compare results against SLAs.






7.0 Develop
This section outlines how to design and record a performance test using Apache JMeter.
Step 1: Plan and Design the Test Scenario
Identify the key business flows you want to simulate.
Define the load pattern (e.g., number of users, ramp-up time).
Choose test environment and target URLs.




Step 2: Configure Browser for Recording
To capture real browser interactions using JMeter’s HTTP(S) Test Script Recorder, configure your browser to route traffic through JMeter's proxy.
2.1 Open Firefox Browser
2.2 Update Network Settings
a. Navigate to Firefox → Settings
b. Scroll down to Network Settings and click "Settings..."
c. Choose Manual proxy configuration
d. Enter the following values:
HTTP Proxy: 127.0.0.1
Port: 8888
Check: “Also use this proxy for HTTPS”



Step 3: Start Recording in JMeter
3.1 Add HTTP(S) Test Script Recorder
a. In JMeter, right-click on Test Plan → Add → Non-Test Elements → HTTP(S) Test Script Recorder
